  "challenge": "ESCALATE overstates residual ambiguity: the packet already supports a straight REJECT. AR-004 is an objective $50 overcharge (stated $22,562.80 vs subtotal+tax $22,512.80) with no additional_charges line to explain the gap, so the total is simply wrong and should not be paid. IN-003 fires on every SKU (WidgetA 22>15, WidgetB 18>10, GadgetX 9>5); get_item_reference confirms those stock caps and active reference prices, so aggregate demand is unfulfillable from standing inventory. PO-001 only bars auto-approval above $10k (policy: manager approval required)—it does not compel human review when independent HIGH defects already disqualify the bill. Atlas Industrial Supply is an active master vendor since 2019 with matching Net 60 terms, but get_vendor_invoice_history returns zero prior invoices, so there is no established billing pattern that would excuse the math error. PR-003 dual prices are annotated volume discounts and match reference unit prices, and DP-001/prior-invoice found no earlier submission—neither salvages the total. Reject for vendor correction of the $50 discrepancy (and stock/PO coverage); do not leave an open escalate.",
  "proposed_outcome": "REJECT",
  "cites_finding_codes": ["AR-004", "IN-003", "PO-001"]
}
